---
description: Jurexio module specifications and registries — use when designing, coding or reviewing any Jurexio module, gate, event, permission or interface
globs: ["**/*.ts","**/*.tsx","**/*.py","**/*.sql","**/*.json"]
alwaysApply: false
---
- The behaviour of each module is defined in `jurexio-specs/specs/Mxx-*.md`. Read the module's spec before writing or changing its code; read only the modules involved.
- Use `jurexio-specs/registry/*.json` (adopted v1) for gate IDs, event names, permission IDs, interface-contract fields and platform constants. Never invent names in application code. If the registry is missing an entry, stop and propose a registry amendment (new row with `status: adopted` only after CTO review + `validate.py`).
- Every gate must record approved, rejected and withdrawn outcomes with a mandatory rejection reason, and enforce its class (GUARDED, DUAL, SELF_ATTESTED).
- Agents never act: AI code may only produce drafts or suggestions that a human approves. Never add an automatic send, approve, file, pay or delete path for AI output.
- Access checks go through the central access decision (CommandCentre); never re-implement access rules inside a module.
- Every state change writes a Ledger event through the outbox, in the same transaction.
- Only India and the US are live jurisdictions in v1.0; never hard-code a jurisdiction — read it from the Jurisdiction Pack.
- Changing a frozen interface contract field is a breaking change: stop and ask.
- Run `python jurexio-specs/registry/validate.py` after editing any registry file.
